          </p>

          <p>
            Its weak points are the ones our scoring picks up. A 20 g scoop at about 74% protein by weight means you need more powder per gram of protein, and at about $2.71 per 25 g in the largest bag it is one of the dearer isolates we track. The third-party testing claim names no certifier, and the coconut milk powder rules it out for anyone avoiding coconut. Together that gives it a Label Score of 48 out of 100.
          </p>

