            Isopure Zero Carb is the better buy for most people choosing between these two brands. It puts 25 g of protein and 0 g of carbs in one scoop, costs about $2.04 per 25 g against about $2.71 for Clean Simple Eats, and scores 63 to 48 on our Label Score. The same pattern holds for the clear wheys, where Isopure Clear undercuts Clean Simple Eats Clear by about a dollar per 25 g.
